<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chlothar II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">584–629</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Clotaire II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chlothar II was a Merovingian king, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chilperic-i">Chilperic I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fredegund">Fredegund</a>, who became King of Neustria as an infant in 584. In 613 he defeated and executed Queen Brunhild and reunited the whole Frankish realm. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edict-of-paris">Edict of Paris</a> of 614 confirmed the rights of nobles and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a>, and he gave Austrasia its own subordinate king.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chlothar-ii.jpg" alt="Chlothar II" width="320" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PHGCOM · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clothaire_II_584_628.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
